<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11961" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cuppēdĭnārĭus</span></b> 
			(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cūp-</span></b> ),
			a, um, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>adj., of</i> or <i>pertaining to
				dainty dishes</i> or <i>delicacies</i>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Forum,</span>”
				<i>a place in Rome</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Symm. Ep. 8, 19</span></i>
			; cf. 2. cuppedo, and cuppes, II.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cuppēdĭnārĭus</span></b> ,
				ii, m., <i>he who
				prepares delicacies</i> or <i>tidbits, a
				confectioner</i>, <i><span class="en">Ter. Eun. 2, 2, 25</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Lampr. Heliog. 30</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
